open 24/7/365 for emergencies. Technicians hold IICRC certifications, and the company partners with nationally recognized testing labs for analysis and written cleanup plans. Franchises like ServiceMaster Restoration by Century (2008 start, 15,000+ jobs done) show solid regional history.</p>\n<p>Best For: Homeowners and commercial property owners across Texas needing 24/7 nationally backed service with IICRC-certified techs, insurance help, and multi-metro coverage.</p>\n<p>Standout Feature: 24/7/365 emergency service backed by a 65+ year national network, and preferred provider status with major insurers to simplify claims.</p>\n<h3 id=\"3-o2-mold-testing\"><strong>3. O2 Mold Testing</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Founded:</strong> Started in 2005 in Reston, VA; run by Green Cleaning Systems, Inc.; now serves Dallas-Fort Worth area.</li>\n<li><strong>Texas Coverage:</strong> Dallas-Fort Worth office at Hi Line Dr, Dallas, TX 75207; serves Frisco, Irving, Garland, Plano, McKinney, Allen, The Colony, and nearby DFW communities.</li>\n<li><strong>Credentials:</strong> Team certified as CMI, IAQA, IICRC BMI, and ACAC.</li>\n<li><strong>Testing Model:</strong> Testing only, no cleanup work; all samples to independent certified labs to avoid conflicts; standard results in 5 business days.</li>\n<li><strong>Rush Service:</strong> Rush results in 24 to 48 hours for extra fee ($150 up to 5 samples; $225 for more); photo estimates before scheduling.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Company Overview: O2 Mold Testing launched in 2005 in Reston, VA and now covers Dallas-Fort Worth through a national operation by Green Cleaning Systems, Inc., dispatching from Dallas, TX 75207 across DFW. The team holds CMI, IAQA, IICRC BMI, and ACAC certifications and runs strictly testing-only, sending every sample to independent certified labs with zero remediation offered to prevent bias. Standard results take 5 business days; rush service returns results in 24 to 48 hours for a fee.</p>\n<p>Best For: DFW homeowners and managers wanting unbiased testing-only inspection from a nationally credentialed provider, with rush 24 to 48 hour lab results if needed.</p>\n<p>Standout Feature: Testing-only approach with CMI, IAQA, IICRC BMI, and ACAC credentials, the only company here offering rush lab results in 24 to 48 hours from an independent certified laboratory.</p>\n<h3 id=\"4-texas-mold-inspectors\"><strong>4. Texas Mold Inspectors</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Location:</strong> Serves Greater Houston, TX and nearby areas; handles residential and commercial jobs; available during and after hours for urgent cases.</li>\n<li><strong>Licensing:</strong> Texas TDLR-licensed Mold Assessment Consultants; follows TMARR rules; assessment and cleanup done by completely separate licensed parties per Texas law.</li>\n<li><strong>No-Referral Policy:</strong> Never refers clients to contractors for fees, removes financial motives that could skew findings.</li>\n<li><strong>Services:</strong> Visual inspection; indoor/outdoor air sampling; wall cavity sampling; tape lift, swab, vacuum, and qPCR-DNA wipe samples (for legal or medical cases); moisture detection; written reports; cleanup protocols; clearance testing.</li>\n<li><strong>Background:</strong> Started by mold survivors, owners Josh and Emily survived toxic mold illness and use that experience to help and teach clients.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Company Overview: Texas Mold Inspectors covers Greater Houston as a TDLR-licensed assessment-only company started by Josh and Emily, who both survived toxic mold illness, a background that shapes their client-first, education-focused service. The company follows a strict no-referral policy, meaning they never send clients to cleanup contractors for kickbacks, keeping findings free from financial pressure. Services include the full range of Texas-approved sampling methods like qPCR-DNA wipes for lawsuits, with written reports and cleanup protocols delivered to clients.</p>\n<p>Best For: Houston homeowners, renters, and tenants facing landlord issues or health worries who need a TDLR-licensed, conflict-free assessment from inspectors who lived through toxic mold illness.</p>\n<p>Standout Feature: Founded by mold survivors with a strict no-referral policy, the only company in this guide where the inspection team’s firsthand mold experience directly shapes how they help and educate clients.</p>\n<h3 id=\"5-fdp-mold-remediation\"><strong>5. FDP Mold Remediation</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Experience:</strong> 20+ years cleaning up mold; IICRC-certified in Mold Remediation and Water Damage Restoration; licensed and insured.</li>\n<li><strong>Texas Coverage:</strong> Dallas office at Garden Brook Dr, Farmers Branch, TX 75234; covers Dallas, Irving, Mesquite, Garland, Grand Prairie, and nearby areas; open Monday to Sunday, all day.</li>\n<li><strong>Availability:</strong> 24/7 emergency cleanup response; written estimates within one business day after on-site visit; free phone consultations before you commit.</li>\n<li><strong>Services:</strong> Inspection; air and surface sampling; written cleanup plan; full mold removal; containment and HEPA filtration; moisture source repair; post-treatment; water damage restoration.</li>\n<li><strong>Estimates:</strong> Photo estimates before on-site visits; on-site visit generates detailed written estimate within one business day.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Company Overview: FDP Mold Remediation is a multi-state IICRC-certified company with 20+ years of mold cleanup experience serving Dallas, TX from its Farmers Branch office, open Monday to Sunday with 24/7 emergency response. The company holds IICRC certifications in both Mold Remediation and Water Damage Restoration, offers free phone consultations before commitment, and delivers detailed written estimates within one business day after on-site inspection. Submit photos on their website for a preliminary estimate before scheduling.</p>\n<p>Best For: Dallas homeowners and commercial owners needing 24/7 IICRC-certified full-service cleanup covering inspection, containment, removal, moisture repair, and post-treatment from one licensed, insured provider.</p>\n<p>Standout Feature: 24/7 full-service emergency response with IICRC certification in both Mold Remediation and Water Damage Restoration, one contractor for inspection, containment, removal, and moisture fixes, seven days a week.</p>\n<h2 id=\"factors-to-consider-when-choosing-a-mold-inspection-company\"><strong>Factors to Consider When Choosing a Mold Inspection Company in Texas</strong></h2>\n<h3 id=\"verify-active-tdlr-mac-licensing-before-scheduling\"><strong>Verify Active TDLR MAC Licensing Before Scheduling</strong></h3>\n<p>Texas law says all mold assessors must hold a current TDLR Mold Assessment Consultant (MAC) license. Check any company’s license directly on the TDLR website before booking. Unlicensed assessments are illegal in Texas, and reports from unlicensed inspectors won’t hold up in real estate deals or insurance claims.</p>\n<h3 id=\"testing-only-vs-full-service-know-the-difference\"><strong>Testing-Only vs. Full-Service (Know the Difference)</strong></h3>\n<p>Texas law stops the same company from doing both your assessment and your cleanup on the same property. Testing-only companies avoid this conflict completely. Full-service companies do both but must keep assessment and cleanup legally separate. Ask which model the company uses, and confirm the person writing your cleanup plan is legally separate from the crew removing the mold.</p>\n<h3 id=\"same-day-vs-standard-turnaround-for-your-situation\"><strong>Same-Day vs. Standard Turnaround for Your Situation</strong></h3>\n<p>Same-day reports matter for closings, active water damage, or health scares. Standard 3 to 5 business day turnarounds work fine for routine checks. Ask the company’s normal turnaround time before you book, and check rush fees if you need faster results.</p>\n<h3 id=\"geographic-coverage-within-texas\"><strong>Geographic Coverage Within Texas</strong></h3>\n<p>Not every company covers the whole state. Some focus on DFW only, others stick to Houston and nearby counties, and national franchises run separate local offices with their own scheduling. Confirm the company you call has a Texas-licensed inspector who can physically visit your property, not just a call center booking for a far-away office.</p>\n<h3 id=\"red-flags-in-mold-assessment\"><strong>Red Flags in Mold Assessment</strong></h3>\n<p>Watch out for companies testing and cleaning without separating those jobs, that violates Texas law. Companies giving verbal results without written reports aren’t following Texas rules. Companies pushing you to start cleanup right away without a written plan from a licensed assessor should raise concerns. Texas TMARR rules require a written cleanup plan before removal work starts.</p>\n<h2 id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n<p>Before hiring any mold inspector in Texas, check their current TDLR MAC license on the TDLR.Texas.gov website. A licensed assessment protects you legally if disputes come up with landlords, insurers, or contractors.</p>\n<p>If you’re dealing with active water damage, choose companies with 24/7 emergency service and same-day written estimates. Waiting 48 hours after water exposure lets mold spread much further.</p>\n<p>Ask for a written cleanup plan before you approve any removal work. Texas TMARR rules require cleanup to follow a written plan from a licensed assessor. Skipping this leaves you unprotected if the contractor’s work gets questioned later.</p>",
